Bus positions are deterministic, which is what makes the output diffable and the tests meaningful. A general force-directed layout would be overkill for a one-line diagram and would not be reproducible. Buses are assigned a depth equal to their shortest path from the slack bus (after excluding out-of-service branches), sorted by (depth, id), and filled into a grid column by column. So the slack bus is leftmost and the network reads left to right, the way a one-line diagram is normally read. Buses not connected to the reference are placed after them rather than dropped. use tpt_nrg_core::EnergySystem;
